CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*list->map)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct drm_map_list)...)
#61: FILE: drivers/staging/gma500/gem_glue.c:65:
+	list->map = kzalloc(sizeof(struct drm_map_list), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:COMPARISON_TO_NULL: Comparison to NULL could be written "!list->map"
#62: FILE: drivers/staging/gma500/gem_glue.c:66:
+	if (list->map == NULL)

Comparisons to NULL in the form (foo == NULL) or (foo != NULL)
are better written as (!foo) and (foo).

